---
const layers = [
  {
    name: 'Application / product architecture',
    tone: 'product',
    items: ['Domain state', 'Feature composition', 'Data ownership', 'Product policy', 'UX-specific behavior'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Framework / meta-framework',
    tone: 'framework',
    items: ['Rendering coordination', 'Scheduling policy', 'Routing conventions', 'Data loading', 'SSR / hydration', 'Compilation'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Standardized runtime primitives',
    tone: 'boundary',
    items: ['Custom Elements', 'Potential Signals', 'Navigation primitives', 'View Transitions', 'DOM update primitives', 'Common controls'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Browser platform',
    tone: 'platform',
    items: ['HTML / DOM', 'CSS', 'JavaScript', 'Networking', 'Storage', 'Rendering / accessibility APIs'],
  },
];
---

<figure class="boundary-map not-prose">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Responsibility map</p>
    <h3>The interesting question is where the boundary moves.</h3>
    <p class="dek">
      Native primitives can absorb stable mechanisms without absorbing the application policy that frameworks coordinate above them.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="stack">
    {layers.map((layer, index) => (
      <>
        <section class:list={['layer', 'tone-' + layer.tone]}>
          <div class="layer-heading">
            <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <strong>{layer.name}</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="chips">
            {layer.items.map((item) => <span>{item}</span>)}
          </div>
        </section>

        {index === 1 && (
          <div class="moving-boundary">
            <span>Moving boundary</span>
            <div aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <strong>mature mechanisms can migrate downward</strong>
          </div>
        )}
      </>
    ))}
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    Platform growth does not imply framework extinction. It can change what frameworks need to implement themselves.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .boundary-map {
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 0.8rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .boundary-map :global(p),
  .boundary-map :global(h3) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 1.35rem 1.45rem;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .layer-heading span,
  .moving-boundary {
    font-family: var(--font-mono-ui);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: 0.45rem !important;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.8rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .dek {
    margin-top: 0.5rem !important;
    max-width: 43rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .layer {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .layer-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.6rem;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .layer-heading span {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.48rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .layer-heading strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .chips span {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    padding: 0.38rem 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .tone-framework {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-primary) 2%, var(--bg-card));
  }

  .tone-boundary {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 5%, var(--bg-card));
  }

  .tone-boundary .layer-heading span,
  .tone-boundary .layer-heading strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .tone-boundary .chips span {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, var(--border-subtle));
  }

  .moving-boundary {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(2rem, 1fr);
    gap: 0.65rem;
    align-items: center;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    padding: 0.55rem 1.15rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.46rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
  }

  .moving-boundary div {
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), transparent);
  }

  .moving-boundary strong {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.43rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
  }

  figcaption {
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .layer {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(13rem, 0.7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr);
      align-items: start;
      gap: 1.3rem;
      padding: 1rem 1.35rem;
    }

    .moving-boundary {
      grid-template-columns: auto minmax(4rem, 1fr) auto;
      padding-inline: 1.35rem;
    }

    .moving-boundary strong {
      grid-column: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
